  "prefLabel": "Pdab 201.06 Appearances Before The Board For Non-Adjudicative Hearings",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pdab 201.06 Appearances Before The Board For Non-Adjudicative Hearings.\n\n(a) A person or party may appear before the board in person, through a representative, or both.\n\n(b) A person or party, excluding individuals providing public testimony, may request to appear before the board provided the request shall be made to the board at least 10 days prior to scheduled board meeting pursuant to Pdab 202.05.\n\n(c) Notwithstanding (b) above, a person or party may request to appear at a date later than the next scheduled board meeting.\n\n(d) The board shall set its own agenda, including, but not limited to, the matters it hears and discusses and the timing of said hearings and discussions.\n\nSource. #13500-A, eff 12-2-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pdab100-300.html"
